  "verdict": "Discrimination is good (RF AUC 0.822 / LR AUC 0.843; PR-AUC 0.229 / 0.265 vs 4.9% base rate) but raw probabilities are grossly miscalibrated by construction: class_weight='balanced' inflates mean predicted risk to 0.338 (RF) / 0.312 (LR) vs a 4.87% observed rate, ECE 0.289 / 0.263 and Hosmer-Lemeshow p<0.001. After the base-rate prior correction (p/(p+(1-p)w)) ECE drops to 0.012 (RF) / 0.010 (LR), Brier 0.0435 / 0.0410 and calibration slopes 1.26 / 0.88 with intercepts 1.04 / -0.25 -> LR is essentially calibrated post-correction (slope~1, HL p=0.058), RF remains slightly under-dispersed (slope 1.26). Both models are therefore usable for ranking, not for absolute risk without recalibration."
