 "caveats": [
  "BP semantics differ across cohorts (diastolic in Diabetes/CKD vs systolic trestbps in HeartUCI) - coefficients are per 1 within-cohort SD, not per mmHg.",
  "84.8% of BP cells are structurally/imputationally missing (absent for all Stroke rows), so the BP coefficient is attenuated toward 0 relative to its complete-case value (0.190 primary vs 0.206 complete-case) and has the widest credible interval.",
  "Stroke contributes 84.1% of rows; the global coefficients are therefore predominantly stroke-driven (see S4/S5).",
  "No PyMC/Stan available: posterior estimated with a hand-written adaptive random-walk Metropolis sampler, cross-validated against a Laplace approximation; results are reproducible from saved draws/seeds (11,22,33,44,55,66)."
